Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage
------------------------------------------
• NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_TRIPS  
  - "starttime" / "stoptime": trip date‑time → to link every ride to the correct GSOD 2014 weather record.  
  - "start_station_latitude", "start_station_longitude": geocode the trip origin → create a GEOGRAPHY/GEOMETRY point to find containing ZIP polygon.  
  - "end_station_latitude", "end_station_longitude": geocode the trip destination → same purpose for destination ZIP.  
  - "tripduration": compute average duration (in seconds → ÷ 60).  

• NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES  
  - "zip_code_geom": polygon geometry of each ZIP → ST_WITHIN(point, zip_code_geom) to translate a coordinate into a ZIP code.  
  - "zip_code": resulting ZIP identifier (TEXT).  
  - "state_code": keep only NY & NJ ZIPs around NYC.  

• NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.CYCLISTIC.ZIP_CODES  
  - "zip": numeric ZIP identifier (same logical key as "zip_code").  
  - "borough": borough name.  
  - "neighborhood": neighborhood name → final grouping columns.  

• NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NOAA_GSOD.GSOD2014  
  - "stn" & "wban": station identifiers → filter to Central Park station.  
  - "year","mo","da": calendar date to join with trip start date.  
  - "temp": mean temperature (°F) → convert to °C/°F as needed.  
  - "wdsp": mean wind speed (knots, stored as TEXT) → convert to m s‑1 (× 0.5144).  
  - "prcp": precipitation (inches) → convert to cm (× 2.54).  

• NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NOAA_GSOD.STATIONS  
  - "usaf","wban","name": find Central Park station codes.  

Typical conditions / filters that will be useful
------------------------------------------------
• GSOD2014."stn"='725033' and GSOD2014."wban"='94728'      -- Central Park WBAN (check via query 2).  
• GSOD2014."year"='2014'                                   -- keep 2014 records only.  
• GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES."state_code" IN ('NY','NJ')  -- NYC metro area.  
• CITIBIKE_TRIPS."starttime" between Unix‑µs for 2014‑01‑01 and 2014‑12‑31.  

Exploratory SQL queries (10)
----------------------------

```sql
-- 1) Description: Peek at raw Citibike trips to understand the timestamp & coordinates fields.
SELECT
  "tripduration",
  "starttime",
  "start_station_latitude",
  "start_station_longitude",
  "end_station_latitude",
  "end_station_longitude"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_TRIPS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Find all weather stations whose name looks like Central Park to get its USAF/WBAN codes.
SELECT
  "usaf",
  "wban",
  TRIM("name") AS "station_name",
  "state",
  "lat",
  "lon"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NOAA_GSOD.STATIONS
WHERE "name" ILIKE '%central%park%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Display Central Park GSOD 2014 records to inspect temperature, wind & precipitation columns.
SELECT
  "year","mo","da",
  "temp",
  "wdsp",
  "prcp"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NOAA_GSOD.GSOD2014
WHERE "stn" = '725033'        -- replace with actual codes from query 2
  AND "wban" = '94728'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Show distinct NY & NJ ZIP codes with their geometries that will be used for spatial matching.
SELECT DISTINCT
  "zip_code",
  "state_code",
  "zip_code_geom"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES
WHERE "state_code" IN ('NY','NJ')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Look up borough & neighborhood names in the Cyclistic ZIP dictionary.
SELECT
  "zip",
  "borough",
  "neighborhood"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.CYCLISTIC.ZIP_CODES
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Join the two ZIP tables to make sure their identifiers match (simple equality check).
SELECT
  g."zip_code",
  c."zip",
  c."borough",
  c."neighborhood"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES  g
JOIN NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.CYCLISTIC.ZIP_CODES          c
  ON g."zip_code" = c."zip"::TEXT
WHERE g."state_code" = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Build a GEOGRAPHY point from trip start‑coords and grab the containing NY ZIP.
SELECT
  t."start_station_latitude",
  t."start_station_longitude",
  g."zip_code"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_TRIPS t
JOIN NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES     g
  ON ST_WITHIN(
